prompt:
One transformer block has width $D = 128$, 8 attention heads and an MLP hidden width $D_{ff} = 512$. Count only the following parts:

- the four attention matrices $W_Q, W_K, W_V, W_O$, each of shape $D \times D$, with no biases;
- the two MLP weight matrices $W_1 \in \mathbb{R}^{D\times D_{ff}}$ and $W_2 \in \mathbb{R}^{D_{ff}\times D}$, without their biases;
- the two layer normalizations, each with a scale $\gamma$ and a shift $\beta$ of length $D$.

How many parameters do these parts hold in total?

explanation:
Each input $x_i$ adds $x_i \cdot [3, 1, 2]$ to the output, starting at position $2(i-1)+1$:

- $x_1 = 5$ covers entries 1-3 with $[15, 5, 10]$;
- $x_2 = 1$ covers entries 3-5 with $[3, 1, 2]$;
- $x_3 = 3$ covers entries 5-7 with $[9, 3, 6]$.

The full output is $[15, 5, 13, 1, 11, 3, 6]$. Entry 5 receives the last filter tap of the second stamp ($1 \cdot 2 = 2$) plus the first tap of the third stamp ($3 \cdot 3 = 9$), so $2 + 9 = 11$.

Typical wrong results: using only one of the two overlapping stamps gives 2 or 9; flipping the filter to $[2, 1, 3]$ gives $1\cdot 3 + 3 \cdot 2 = 9$. Overlap-add of the stamps is what makes the entries at the overlaps sums.
